  "findings": [
    "Under the stated uniform weak-composition bridge, let S_h=Y_1+...+Y_h. For 1≤h<R, exact counting gives P(S_h=a | S_R=K) = [C(a+h-1,h-1) C(K-a+R-h-1,R-h-1)] / C(K+R-1,R-1). More generally, conditional on S_h=a, the next ℓ coordinates have total w with probability C(w+ℓ-1,ℓ-1) C(K-a-w+R-h-ℓ-1,R-h-ℓ-1) / C(K-a+R-h-1,R-h-1). This is the required bridge decomposition; it does not introduce independent increments.",
    "At pair time j, h=2j and log_2 z_j=1-{βτ}+S_h-βh. Thus z_j<η iff S_h<βh+c_η, where c_η=log_2(η/z_0) is fixed. Since K=βR+O(1), the bridge mean is hK/R=βh+O(1). Its exact variance is K h(R-h)(K+R)/(R^2(R+1)), which is Θ(R) when h/R stays in a compact subinterval of (0,1). A direct Stirling expansion of the displayed beta-binomial mass gives a centered Gaussian local scale, so at every fixed bulk fraction P(z_j<η | S_R=K)→1/2. Therefore low entries are not an exceptional event.",
    "There is also an exact positive-probability entrance mechanism. If the first d=2L raw coordinates vanish, then z_L=z_0(4/9)^L. Choosing L with 2(4/9)^L<η forces a low entry, while the exact probability is C(K+R-d-1,R-d-1)/C(K+R-1,R-1)→(1+β)^(-d)>0. This supports neither the target estimate nor a refutation, because the target allows low blocks.",
    "The bridge formulas and one-time asymptotics do not control the joint lower tail of low/non-low entries on the disjoint block grid. In particular, they do not establish the required occupation Laplace bound, and they say nothing about the additional bounded-positive and nonresonance marks. No rigorous proof or actual accessible counterexample to the primary claim was obtained."
  ],
  "claim_status": "OPEN",
  "first_missing_step": {
    "inequality": "For some a>0 and C<∞ depending only on the fixed parameters, uniformly over all sufficiently large accessible actual arrays, prove P(Σ_{q∈Q_R} 1_{z_{j_q}≥η} < a log R | S_R=K and exact first-passage data) ≤ C/R.",
    "scope": "This is strictly narrower than the target: it counts only non-low block entries and omits bounded positivity and amplified nonresonance.",
    "why_missing": "The exact bridge decomposition supplies marginals and conditional segment laws, but no joint lower-tail estimate under even-time sampling, rational ties, or the bounded affine threshold. Proving this narrower estimate would still not prove the marked C_q estimate; it is the first unresolved low-state occupation step."
  },
